  "key_evidence": [
    "Abbott agreed on 20 August 2026 to pay $670 million to settle roughly 2,000 lawsuits alleging its preterm-infant formula concealed the risk of necrotizing enterocolitis, a bowel disease with an estimated mortality rate above 20% in premature newborns.",
    "Abbott dropped its appeal of a $495 million jury verdict after a Missouri appeals court upheld that verdict in May 2026 — converting a contested trial-court verdict into a final civil failure-to-warn judgment. This is the single most probative new fact since the 2026-04-20 baseline.",
    "Abbott did not admit liability and stated it remains confident in the safety of its infant formula products, so Harm Acknowledgment (AB1) and Historical Harm Acknowledgment (EQ5) stay at 2.",
    "About 1,700 lawsuits covering up to 12,700 infants remain pending; the August settlement resolves roughly a tenth of claimants.",
    "FAVOURABLE COUNTERWEIGHT, SCORED: Correction Willingness (AB2) rises to 3 because paying and abandoning the appeal is a real course correction after a period of pure denial recorded at the April baseline."
  ],
